NTP-SCTAP is a distributed cybersecurity research platform that demonstrates secure covert communication over the Network Time Protocol (NTP), real-time packet inspection, AES-256-GCM encryption, protocol analysis, and defensive threat detection across multiple hosts.
Distributed Communication
Windows ↔ Linux secure communication
Cross-platform packet transmission
Remote sender client
Real network deployment
Bridged network support
Automatic receiver service
